  "section_notes": "S2 is the main weakening: the 5% limit is effectively replaced by a 6.5% ceiling after a 12-month remediation window, so the Hearth 10 (6.2%) remains sellable. This meets both companies' red lines on per-model disclosure, because buyers get the results and the public does not. S1, S3, S4 and S5 are in the safe or acceptable ranges. S5 keeps a firm 8-per-100k recall trigger, which affects the Ember 8, and S3 and S4 sit at the red-line minimums of 6 years and 36 months."
